{%- comment -%}
  MUTO — Ingredients.

  Artboard band 6223–7250 of NAD.pdf: a four-line 64px heading, two lines on
  the left margin and two on the right, a 426×57 filter pill under it, then the
  ingredients on a four-column grid of 333×75 tiles with a 20 gap — a 14px name,
  a mono dose, a mono group tag and a dashed 30px "+" on the right.

  Each tile is a <details>: the "+" is the disclosure and the body says why the
  ingredient is in the formula. That is the point of the band — the artboard
  shows the closed state, and a label you can't interrogate is the thing this
  page is arguing against. No JS is needed to open one.

  The filter is a group of toggle buttons, not a tablist: four tabs over one
  panel is not a tablist, and each button is a predicate over the same list
  rather than a different view. It is rendered hidden and revealed by the
  script, so with JS off the page shows every ingredient rather than a control
  that does nothing.

  BLOCKS, one per ingredient, so the formula can change without a code change.
  Shopify caps a section at 50 blocks; the formula is 19.

  MOBILE: one column rather than four, capped at three tiles and scrolling
  inside itself, with a position indicator under it. Three across left each
  name about 88px and broke half of them mid-word; a stacked list of nineteen
  is a band you scroll past rather than read.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'muto-crea.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'muto-crea.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  assign spt = section.settings.space_top | default: 100 | times: 0.01
  assign spb = section.settings.space_bottom | default: 100 | times: 0.01
  assign heading_id = 'mc-ing-' | append: section.id
  assign groups = section.blocks | map: 'settings' | map: 'group' | uniq
-%}

<div class="mc mc--ing mc--fit-{{ section.settings.fit | default: 'crea' }}" style="--mc-spt:{{ spt }};--mc-spb:{{ spb }}">
  <div class="mc__wrap">
    <section class="mc__ing" aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}" data-mc-ing>
      {%- assign mc_lines = section.settings.heading | escape | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
      {%- assign mc_right = section.settings.heading_right | escape | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
      <h2 class="mc__h2 mc__ing-head" id="{{ heading_id }}">
        {%- for mc_line in mc_lines %}
          <span class="mc__head-line">{{ mc_line }}</span>
        {% endfor -%}
        {%- for mc_line in mc_right %}
          <span class="mc__head-line mc__head-line--right">{{ mc_line }}</span>
        {% endfor -%}
      </h2>
      {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
        {%- assign mc_lede = section.settings.lede | escape | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
        <div class="mc__ing-lede">
          {%- for mc_line in mc_lede -%}
            <p class="mc__prob-lede">{{ mc_line | strip }}</p>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if groups.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="mc__tabs mc__rail mc__ing-filter" role="group"
          aria-label="{{ section.settings.filter_label | default: 'Filter ingredients by what they do' | escape }}"
          data-mc-ing-filter hidden>
          <button type="button" class="mc__tab" aria-pressed="true" data-mc-ing-group="">
            {{- section.settings.all_label | default: 'All' -}}
          </button>
          {%- for group in groups -%}
            {%- if group != blank -%}
              <button type="button" class="mc__tab" aria-pressed="false" data-mc-ing-group="{{ group | escape }}">
                {{- group -}}
              </button>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <ul class="mc__ing-list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <li class="mc__ing-item" data-mc-ing-item="{{ block.settings.group | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <details class="mc__ing-row">
              <summary class="mc__ing-sum">
                <span class="mc__ing-main">
                  <span class="mc__ing-name">{{ block.settings.name }}</span>
                  <span class="mc__ing-meta">
                    {%- if block.settings.dose != blank -%}
                      <span class="mc__ing-dose">{{ block.settings.dose }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- if block.settings.group != blank -%}
                      <span class="mc__ing-group">{{ block.settings.group }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                </span>
                {%- comment -%}
                  Last in source on purpose. At phone width the tile is three to
                  a row and about 88px of text wide, and the "+" is floated: put
                  it first and it shortens the first line, which turns half
                  these names into mid-word breaks. Put it last and it floats to
                  the bottom-right corner instead, leaving every line of the
                  name the full width. The desktop row lays it out as a flex
                  item on the right, where source order is what it wants anyway.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <span class="mc__ing-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>
              {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                <div class="mc__ing-body mc__rt">{{ block.settings.text }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </details>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%}
        The list is capped to three tiles and scrolls at phone width, so it
        gets a position indicator under it. It ships without the attribute the
        stylesheet shows it on: the script adds that only after measuring a
        list that really does overflow, which is never the case on the desktop
        grid and need not be the case once the filter has narrowed the list.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="mc__ing-scroll" data-mc-ing-scroll aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="mc__ing-scroll-thumb" data-mc-ing-thumb></span>
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.foot != blank -%}
        <p class="mc__ing-foot">{{ section.settings.foot }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "MUTO — Ingredients",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "mc-section",
  "max_blocks": 50,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Nineteen ingredients.\nOne system." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "heading_right", "label": "Heading, right margin", "default": "Beneath energy,\nrecovery & healthy ageing.", "info": "Lines typed here sit on the right margin under the ones above, at every width." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lede", "label": "Subheading", "info": "Optional. Each line is its own paragraph under the heading." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "all_label", "label": "\"All\" filter label", "default": "All" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_label", "label": "Filter group label", "default": "Filter ingredients by what they do", "info": "Read aloud by a screen reader, not shown on the page." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "foot", "label": "Footnote" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "fit", "label": "Which wash", "default": "crea", "options": [{ "value": "crea", "label": "Creatine page" }, { "value": "nad", "label": "NAD+ page" }], "info": "The mint wash is least-squares fitted to one artboard's own pixels, and the two product pages wash this band differently." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "space_top", "label": "Space above", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 100 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "space_bottom", "label": "Space below", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 100 }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "ingredient",
      "name": "Ingredient",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name", "default": "Nicotinamide riboside" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "dose", "label": "Dose", "default": "300mg" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "group", "label": "Group", "default": "Produce", "info": "Tiles are filtered by this. Ingredients sharing a group share a filter button." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Why it's in the formula" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "MUTO — Ingredients",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Nicotinamide riboside", "dose": "300mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "A direct NAD+ precursor: your cells convert it in two steps. 300mg is the dose the published human work is built on, not a fraction of it." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Trimethylglycine", "dose": "450mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "A methyl donor. NAD+ metabolism uses methyl groups up, so TMG puts them back rather than leaving the rest of the pathway competing for them." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin D3", "dose": "2000IU", "group": "Produce", "text": "Most people in the UK run low between October and March. Included at a daily dose rather than a token one." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin K2 (MK-7)", "dose": "100µg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Pairs with D3: K2 directs calcium towards bone rather than soft tissue. The MK-7 form stays in circulation longest." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B1 (Thiamin)", "dose": "5mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Part of the enzyme set that turns what you eat into cellular energy." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin)", "dose": "5mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "The precursor to FAD, one of the two carriers the energy pathway runs on. NAD+ is the other." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B3 (Niacin)", "dose": "16mg NE", "group": "Produce", "text": "A second route into NAD+, alongside nicotinamide riboside, at the EU reference intake." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B5", "dose": "10mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Pantothenic acid, which builds coenzyme A — the molecule that feeds fuel into the citric acid cycle." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B6 (P5P)", "dose": "5mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "The active form, so it needs no conversion in the liver before it can be used." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Folate", "dose": "400µg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Works with B12 and TMG in the methyl cycle, which is the cycle NAD+ metabolism draws on." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Vitamin B12", "dose": "100µg", "group": "Produce", "text": "The other half of the methyl cycle. Absorption falls with age, so the dose is set above the reference intake." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Biotin", "dose": "300µg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Cofactor for the enzymes that handle fats and amino acids." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Zinc (bisglycinate)", "dose": "15mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Chelated for absorption, and easier on an empty stomach than the oxide form." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Copper (bisglycinate)", "dose": "1mg", "group": "Produce", "text": "Balances the zinc. A daily zinc dose without copper beside it depletes copper over time." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Grapeseed extract", "dose": "150mg", "group": "Protect", "text": "Polyphenols, standardised rather than a whole-fruit powder, so the dose on the label means something." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Trans-resveratrol", "dose": "50mg", "group": "Protect", "text": "The trans isomer specifically — the form the research uses, and the one that survives the shelf." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Coenzyme Q10", "dose": "150mg", "group": "Put to work", "text": "Carries electrons inside the mitochondria. Levels fall from your thirties onwards, and statins lower them further." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "PQQ", "dose": "20mg", "group": "Put to work", "text": "Studied for its role in mitochondrial biogenesis: making new mitochondria rather than only running the ones you have." } },
        { "type": "ingredient", "settings": { "name": "Bioperine®", "dose": "5mg", "group": "Put to work", "text": "Black pepper extract. It is here because it improves the absorption of several of the ingredients above." } }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product", "page", "index"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
